# {{ package_name }}

{{ project_description }}

This package resolves deferred field references for the `{{ provider_scheme }}` URI
scheme. It exposes only an `invoke_toolkit.field_resolver` entry point; it does
not expose an invoke-toolkit task collection.

## Development

```bash
uv sync
uv run pytest
```

Implement `{{ package_slug }}.resolve`. Invoke-toolkit calls it once per task
invocation with all omitted fields that use the `{{ provider_scheme }}://` scheme.
Return a mapping containing exactly one final value for every request parameter.
A request provides the parameter name, complete URI reference, and annotation;
providers may use the annotation to return typed values such as `pathlib.Path`.

Install this provider in the same environment as the consumer application after
implementing and testing it.

## Resolver contract

```python
from collections.abc import Mapping, Sequence
from typing import Any

from invoke_toolkit import Context, FieldResolutionRequest


def resolve(
    ctx: Context,
    requests: Sequence[FieldResolutionRequest],
) -> Mapping[str, Any]:
    ...
```

Do not log URI references or resolved values when they can contain secrets.

